## 🎯 Part 2: Extracting UIDs & Balance Data from Live WebSockets
Once you generate your extracted_frames.txt log from live casino gameplay streams, the file will contain thousands of raw text lines. To pull the critical user identifiers (UIDs), session tracking contexts, and balance strings out of the mess, use this custom terminal parsing pipeline on your machine.
## Step 1: Automated Token & UID Isolate Command
Run this unified sed and grep filter chain directly inside your terminal workspace to isolate session security states from the raw text stream:

# Extract user accounts, financial metrics, and active session tokens
grep -oEi '"(user_id|uid|player_id|token|session|jwt)":"[^" ]+"' extracted_frames.txt | sort -u

## Step 2: The WebSocket State Ledger Builder
To see exactly how the application updates balance values dynamically across transactions, format the raw frames structurally using awk to view the timeline:

# Pull timestamps, wagers, and ending balance metrics into a readable terminal ledger
grep -E "(balance|bet|payout|win)" extracted_frames.txt | awk -F',' '{
    for(i=1;i<=NF;i++) {
        if($i ~ /"uid"/ || $i ~ /"balance"/ || $i ~ /"amount"/) {
            print $i
        }
    }
    print "---"
}' | head -n 30

